  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Fetal Alcohol Syndrome is a common congenital disorder caused by maternal alcohol consumption during pregnancy. Patients presents with physical and mental developmental delay.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made by typical clinical features present at birth in the setting of maternal alcohol consumption during pregnancy.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is a multidisciplinary approach to address orthopedic, neurological, and developmental abnormalities.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
